<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining raises copper price by 20,000 yen.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining raises copper price by 20,000 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said on Monday it was raising its selling price for electrolytic copper by 20,000 yen to 330,000 yen per tonne, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Major Japanese smelters periodically review their selling prices, changing them in line with market prices and currency rates.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
